   "text": "I read the drawing as a branched, dendrimer-like structure built from aspartic-acid units joined by hexamethylene (\u2013(CH2)6\u2013) linkers. I traced it unit by unit from the centre outwards.\n\n**Units and linkers**\n- Each aspartic unit has an \u03b1-carbon carrying an NH\u2013hexyl arm, a C(=O) group and a CH2C(=O) group. Each hexyl arm ends in NH2 or in an amide/amine link to the next unit.\n- The central unit is drawn with a C=O attached directly to a carbon chain rather than to an NH. I kept it as drawn: C(=O)\u2013(CH2)6\u2013NH, with the NH forming an amide to the next unit.\n- Every linker chain counted as six carbons. The central C(=O) chain is also six CH2 plus the carbonyl, though that count is a little less certain from the pixel spacing.\n\n**Branches from the central unit**\n- **Left branch.** Through an NH\u2013hexyl link it reaches a second aspartic unit. That unit carries an amide\u2013hexyl\u2013NH\u2013(aspartic unit bearing CH2COOH) arm on one side and, on the other, a second terminal unit with two NH\u2013hexyl\u2013NH2 arms.\n- **Right branch.** The central chain's NH forms an amide to another aspartic unit, which splits into two further sub-branches.\n  - The first sub-branch leads through an aspartic unit with a COOH group and a terminal diamine unit.\n  - The second sub-branch leads through a unit bearing a COOH-terminated aspartic arm and a diamine unit.\n\nAll stereocentres are drawn with plain bonds, so no stereochemistry is specified. I wrote the SMILES by hand and checked the counts of hexyl chains and the amide and amine linkages against the drawing, but I did not run it through a parser.\n\nSMILES: NCCCCCCNC(=O)CC(NCCCCCCNC(C(=O)NCCCCCCNC(=O)C(NCCCCCCN)CC(=O)NCCCCCCN)CC(=O)NCCCCCCNC(CC(=O)O)C(=O)NCCCCCCN)C(=O)CCCCCCNC(=O)C(NCCCCCCNC(=O)C(NCCCCCCN)CC(=O)NCCCCCCNC(CC(=O)NCCCCCCNC(=O)C(NCCCCCCN)CC(=O)NCCCCCCN)C(=O)O)CC(=O)NCCCCCCNC(C(=O)NCCCCCCNC(=O)C(NCCCCCCN)CC(=O)NCCCCCCN)CC(=O)NCCCCCCNC(=O)CC(NCCCCCCN)C(=O)O"
